  "html": "<p>Poland quietly became a nicotine pouch powerhouse, and its two flagship exports could not think more differently. 77 (Luna Corporate / Tobacco Concept Factory) bet everything on consistency. CUBA (Nicotobacco Factory) bet everything on range. Same country, same slim format, opposite worldviews.</p><h2>77: one strength, every flavour</h2><p>The 77 pitch is radical in its simplicity: essentially the whole line runs at <strong>10.4mg per pouch (16mg/g)</strong>, slim, 20 pouches, 13g per can. Strength is a settled question — the entire brand experience is choosing between 15+ flavours. And the flavours are the point: <a href=\"/product/77-apple-mint-medium\">Apple Mint</a> with its succulent-orchard-fruit brief, Cola in three variants, Watermelon Ice, Black Currant, the dessert outlier <a href=\"/search?q=77+salted+caramel+medium\">Salted Caramel</a>, and the category's most convincing tobacco-flavoured (yet tobacco-free) pouch in Classic Tobacco. Our research repeatedly surfaces 77's quality story — medical-grade nicotine, food-grade flavourings — and an anti-pretension streak: this is a brand for people who've decided their strength and want an interesting rotation.</p><p>One honest labelling note: 77 calls 10.4mg \"Medium\" on its own 3/5 scale, while most retailers class it extra strong. Trust the number, not the adjective.</p><h2>CUBA: one name, the whole spectrum</h2><p>CUBA's pitch is the opposite: pick your intensity, then your flavour. Three tiers span a 4× range — <strong>White at 10.4mg</strong> (<a href=\"/product/cuba-white-apple-juice\">Apple Juice</a> leads it), <strong>Ninja at 15.6mg</strong> with 25 pouches per can and the playful flavour bench (Bubble Gum, Energy, Pinacolada), and <strong>Black at 43mg</strong> (<a href=\"/product/cuba-black-cold-dry\">Cold Dry</a> and a dozen fruit variants) wearing its \"Don't Go There\" warning like a badge. Where 77 removes a decision, CUBA adds one — and makes the decision itself the brand experience.</p><h2>Head to head where they overlap</h2><p>At 10.4mg the two brands meet directly: 77's full range vs CUBA White. The differences are texture and tempo. 77's moist pouches run steady 30-minute-plus sessions with even release; CUBA White runs hotter and shorter (20–40 minutes officially), front-loading its flavour. On pure flavour engineering at this tier, 77's breadth is hard to argue with — CUBA keeps its most inventive work for the Ninja tier.</p><h2>Value and cans</h2><p>Both ship slim-format, similar can sizes (13g). CUBA Ninja's 25-pouch cans are the family's value play; 77 keeps a uniform 20 everywhere — consistency again, right down to the count.</p><h2>Which philosophy is yours?</h2><p>Buy <strong>77</strong> if you know your strength and want the most interesting flavour rotation in the strong mainstream — it's the brand equivalent of a well-run kitchen with one fixed menu price. Buy <strong>CUBA</strong> if strength itself is the variable you play with — no other single brand lets you move from a friendly 10.4mg apple to a 43mg warning label without changing logo. Two valid answers; Poland ships both.</p><p><strong>Related reading:</strong> <a href=\"/blog/cuba-black-vs-ninja-vs-white\">CUBA Black vs Ninja vs White</a> · <a href=\"/blog/77-nicotine-pouches-all-flavours-rated\">77 Nicotine Pouches: All Flavours Rated</a> · <a href=\"/blog/cola-nicotine-pouches-guide\">Cola Pouches Guide</a></p>",
