  "html": "<p>Beyond the tobacco-giant brands sits a second generation of pouch makers who grew up all-white — no tobacco heritage to translate, just a blank sheet. ACE (Ministry of Snus, Denmark) and CLEW (USA) are the two most interesting of them, and they've specialised in opposite virtues: ACE in range discipline, CLEW in mouthfeel.</p><h2>ACE: Danish precision with a wild streak</h2><p>Ministry of Snus builds ACE like a pharmacist with a sense of humour. The core range is clean and legible: <a href=\"/product/ace-cool-mint-low\">ACE Cool Mint Low</a> at 3mg (6mg/g) is one of the best first pouches on the market — smooth, sweet spearmint pitched explicitly at newcomers. <a href=\"/product/ace-eucalyptus\">ACE Eucalyptus</a> (6mg, 12mg/g) is the range's signature eccentric: a herbal, balm-like profile our research file memorably files under \"Tiger Balm in pouch form.\" All slim, all 20 per can.</p><p>Then there's the <strong>ACE X</strong> sub-line — the \"enhanced release\" tier starting at 8mg (16mg/g): <a href=\"/product/ace-x-cool-mint\">ACE X Cool Mint</a> for people who found the core range polite, and ACE X Guarana Chili Boost, an energy-drink-meets-habanero flavour that has no neighbour anywhere in the category. Ski-lodge cool on the outside, occasionally unhinged on the inside.</p><h2>CLEW: the mouthfeel specialists</h2><p>CLEW's reputation — consistent across our research sources — is texture: an ultra-smooth, soft-edged pouch experience that makes its numbers feel gentler than they read. The mid-range trio (<a href=\"/product/clew-cool-mint-10mg\">Cool Mint</a>, Menthol, <a href=\"/product/clew-blueberry-10mg\">Blueberry</a>, all 10mg / 14mg/g, slim, 20 per can) is the brand's centre of gravity, with Menthol notable for running sessions at the long end of the category (45–60 minutes).</p><p>CLEW's structural advantage is the <strong>widest strength range of any single brand we stock: 2.5mg to 20mg</strong>. Five tiers, one house style — you could plausibly spend your entire pouch journey, from first can to seasoned daily use, without leaving the brand. It's also an award-winning line in its home market, a rare American voice in a Nordic-dominated category.</p><h2>Head to head</h2><p><strong>Entry point:</strong> ACE Cool Mint Low (3mg) vs CLEW 2.5mg — both superb; CLEW's is the gentlest number on our shelf, ACE's the more flavour-forward. <strong>Mid-tier:</strong> CLEW's 10mg trio vs ACE X at 8mg — CLEW smoother, ACE X punchier per its enhanced-release design. <strong>Personality:</strong> ACE experiments with flavour (Eucalyptus, Guarana Chili); CLEW perfects delivery. <strong>Range logic:</strong> CLEW is one long ladder; ACE is two brands in a trench coat — the polite core and the X line.</p><h2>The verdict</h2><p>Pick <strong>ACE</strong> for character: distinctive flavours, a friendly floor, and the X line when you're ready. Pick <strong>CLEW</strong> for the smoothest physical experience in the category and a strength ladder you'll never outgrow. Both prove the second generation isn't imitating the giants — it's out-specialising them.</p><p><strong>Related reading:</strong> <a href=\"/blog/best-low-strength-nicotine-pouches\">Best Low-Strength Pouches</a> · <a href=\"/blog/unusual-nicotine-pouch-flavours\">Unusual Flavours Worth Trying</a> · <a href=\"/blog/mint-intensity-map\">The Mint Intensity Map</a></p>",
