  "html": "<p>Sweden gave the world the pouch format — and these two Stockholm-linked brands show how differently \"premium Swedish\" can be interpreted. ZYN is the establishment: Swedish Match heritage, global scale. Après is the challenger: founded 2020, plant-based, flavour-obsessed. Both slim. Both excellent. Very different meals.</p><h2>Scale vs craft</h2><p><strong>ZYN's</strong> credentials are unmatched: 114.1 million cans sold in a single year (2020), the #1 smokefree brand in Sweden, and the de-facto reference product in every mint conversation on earth. When our research calls <a href=\"/product/zyn-cool-mint-slim-s3\">ZYN Cool Mint</a> \"the benchmark,\" it's describing a measurable fact of the market.</p><p><strong>Après</strong> (Après Nicotine AB) answers scale with intent: biodegradable plant-based pouch materials, fully recyclable cans, and a flavour bench that runs to some two dozen entries — including things nobody else attempts, like Lemon Curd and Ice Tea Peach. \"Sweet. Fresh. Swedish.\" is the house line, and the products live up to all three words.</p><h2>The strength architectures</h2><p>ZYN ladders each flavour: 3, 6, 9, 11mg across slim and mini. Après runs four named tiers across its range: Mini (3.2mg), Normal (4.4mg), Extra Strong (~8.3mg — <a href=\"/search?q=apres+cola+extra+strong\">Cola</a> at 8.25mg, Lemon Curd at 8.3mg) and Hyper Strong (11mg). The ceilings are nearly identical (11mg both); the floors are close (3 vs 3.2mg). Strength won't separate these brands — everything else will.</p><h2>Dry vs moist, again — but premium</h2><p>ZYN's dry-surface engineering delivers the longest, most discreet sessions in the category: minimal drip, up to 60 minutes, mini formats for total invisibility. Après goes the other way with high moisture content — flavour onset in the first minute, minimal-drip formulation despite the moisture, sessions in the standard 30–45 band. <a href=\"/search?q=apres+blueberry\">Après Blueberry</a> (4.4mg) is the thesis product: jammy, natural-tasting fruit that arrives instantly and reads closer to a fresh punnet than confectionery.</p><h2>Flavour worldviews</h2><p>ZYN perfects the classics — Cool Mint, Spearmint, and <a href=\"/search?q=zyn+citrus\">Citrus</a>, the market's best-known non-mint pouch. Après treats flavour as the entire adventure: beverage-inspired profiles (Cola, Ice Tea Peach, Tangerine Spritz), dessert experiments (Lemon Curd), and fruit that tastes grown rather than compounded. If ZYN is a perfectly poured espresso, Après is the interesting café that changes its menu.</p><h2>Sustainability</h2><p>Only one of these brands makes it a pillar: Après' biodegradable pouches and recyclable cans are, per our research, baked into the brand rather than bolted on. ZYN's story is quality and scale, not ecology.</p><h2>The verdict</h2><p><strong>ZYN</strong> for benchmark reliability, maximum discretion, and the longest sessions. <strong>Après</strong> for flavour adventure, faster onset, and the greenest materials in the premium tier. The happy discovery: at these price points you're not choosing a compromise either way — just a personality.</p><p><strong>Related reading:</strong> <a href=\"/blog/zyn-vs-velo\">ZYN vs VELO</a> · <a href=\"/blog/best-low-strength-nicotine-pouches\">Best Low-Strength Pouches</a> · <a href=\"/blog/unusual-nicotine-pouch-flavours\">Unusual Flavours Worth Trying</a></p>",
