  "html": "<p>Berry is the flavour family where authenticity shows fastest: the good ones taste like fruit picked this morning, the bad ones like melted sweets. Every pick below passed the real-fruit test in our research — listed from gentlest to strongest.</p><h2>Après Blueberry — 4.4mg, the natural benchmark</h2><p><a href=\"/search?q=apres+blueberry\">Après Blueberry</a> is the berry pouch we measure the others against: juicy wild blueberry with a bright, jammy character and genuine tartness — \"closer to a punnet of fresh-picked berries than a synthetic boiled sweet,\" as our research notes put it. High moisture delivers the fruit in the first minute; 4.4mg keeps it sessionable for anyone. If you're berry-curious, start exactly here.</p><h2>CLEW Blueberry — 10mg, the smooth operator</h2><p><a href=\"/product/clew-blueberry-10mg\">CLEW Blueberry</a> (14mg/g, slim, 20 per can) brings the family into the strong tier with CLEW's signature ultra-smooth mouthfeel. The berry reads rounder and softer than Après' bright take — blueberry with the edges sanded, which suits its longer, gentler sessions.</p><h2>The 77 berry trio — 10.4mg each</h2><p>77 fields three distinct berries at its uniform strength, and the differences are real:</p><p><strong><a href=\"/search?q=77+blueberry+medium\">77 Blueberry</a></strong> — sweet-tart authenticity with a cool icy finish; the everyday pick of the trio. <strong><a href=\"/search?q=77+black+currant+medium\">77 Black Currant</a></strong> — the connoisseur's berry: genuinely sweet <em>and</em> sour like fruit off the bush, plus the best conversation-starter in the category (blackcurrant was banned in the US for most of a century for threatening pine forests — this is a distinctly European flavour). <strong><a href=\"/product/77-arctic-berry-medium\">77 Arctic Berry VB Edition</a></strong> — Nordic forest berries with a clean cooling effect, in the Valtteri Bottas F1 collaboration can; lingonberry tartness gives it the wildest character of the three.</p><h2>CUBA Black Forest Berries — 43mg, the extreme outlier</h2><p><a href=\"/product/cuba-black-forest-berries\">CUBA Black Forest Berries</a> (66mg/g) exists for a different audience entirely: the dark-fruit profile is genuinely good, but it arrives strapped to the strongest nicotine tier in the catalogue and burns through a short, intense 20–30 minute session. Listed for completeness and for the small group who already live at this altitude — the \"Don't Go There\" label is CUBA's own.</p><h2>Choosing your berry</h2><p>For <strong>authenticity</strong>, Après Blueberry and 77 Black Currant are the two that taste most like actual fruit. For <strong>smoothness</strong>, CLEW. For <strong>character</strong>, Arctic Berry's Nordic wildness. For <strong>strength with your fruit</strong>, the 77 trio at 10.4mg covers the strong mainstream, and nobody sensible starts their berry journey at CUBA Black. A pleasant discovery of the research: berry is the family where mid-priced pouches most consistently outperform their price — the flavour chemistry is mature, and it shows.</p><p><strong>Related reading:</strong> <a href=\"/blog/unusual-nicotine-pouch-flavours\">Unusual Flavours Worth Trying</a> · <a href=\"/blog/77-nicotine-pouches-all-flavours-rated\">77 Flavours Rated</a> · <a href=\"/blog/best-low-strength-nicotine-pouches\">Best Low-Strength Pouches</a></p>",
