  "html": "<p>Cola is the most underrated flavour family in nicotine pouches — hard to do well (real cola is acidity, citrus and caramel in balance, not just sweetness) and gloriously nostalgic when a brand pulls it off. This is, as far as we can tell, the UK's only cola-specific pouch guide. Here's the whole field.</p><h2>The 77 cola trio — 10.4mg each</h2><p>Poland's 77 owns this family with three genuinely distinct takes at its uniform strength (16mg/g, slim, 20 per can):</p><p><strong><a href=\"/product/77-cola-medium\">77 Cola</a></strong> — the reference: an intense, tingling, fruity cola with zingy top notes first, caramel depth mid-session and a fresh finish. The slight moisture in the pouch means it gets going the moment it settles.</p><p><strong><a href=\"/product/77-cola-cherry-medium\">77 Cola Cherry</a></strong> — cherry cola done properly: effervescent cola zing up front, ripe dark cherry blooming underneath, sweetness balanced rather than sticky. Cherry that tastes like fruit, not cough syrup — a harder trick than it sounds.</p><p><strong><a href=\"/search?q=77+cola+vanilla+medium\">77 Cola Vanilla</a></strong> — the soda-fountain classic. The vanilla is the clever part: it acts as a counterweight to the nicotine strength, making an extra-strong-classified pouch feel smooth and rounded. The most sessionable of the three.</p><h2>Après Cola Extra Strong — 8.25mg</h2><p>Sweden's answer treats cola as a complete profile: <a href=\"/search?q=apres+cola+extra+strong\">Après No.4</a> delivers acidity, citrus brightness and rounded caramel in deliberate sequence — zingy top notes first, rich sweetness settling mid-session, citrus keeping the finish fresh. High moisture makes it the fastest-arriving cola here, and it's the pick if 10.4mg is more than you want. (The same profile runs from Mini 3.2mg to this Extra Strong tier.)</p><h2>CUBA Black Cola — 43mg</h2><p>The extreme option: <a href=\"/product/cuba-black-cola\">CUBA Black Cola</a> (66mg/g) puts a dark, punchy cola on the strongest platform in the catalogue. The flavour work is real, but be clear about the purchase: this is a 43mg pouch that happens to taste of cola, not a cola experience that happens to be strong. Sessions are short and emphatic, and CUBA's own \"Don't Go There\" tier label applies. CUBA's Ninja tier (15.6mg) covers the middle ground across its playful range if Black is — sensibly — too far.</p><h2>Matching cola to occasion</h2><p>The nostalgic afternoon pouch: 77 Cola Vanilla, the smoothest of the family. The flavour-maximalist choice: 77 Cola Cherry, the most layered. The gentle entry: Après Cola at 8.25mg with the fastest flavour onset. The straight classic: 77 Cola. And the extreme tier: CUBA Black Cola, for the few who already know they belong there.</p><p>One family-wide note: cola pouches reward moist formulas — every entry above uses one, because cola's fizzy illusion depends on quick, bright flavour release. It's the rare family where the dry-pouch giants simply don't compete.</p><p><strong>Related reading:</strong> <a href=\"/blog/77-nicotine-pouches-all-flavours-rated\">77 Flavours Rated</a> · <a href=\"/blog/unusual-nicotine-pouch-flavours\">Unusual Flavours Worth Trying</a> · <a href=\"/blog/77-vs-cuba\">77 vs CUBA</a></p>",
