  "html": "<p>No brand in our catalogue spans the strength spectrum like CUBA. Nicotobacco Factory (Poland) runs three distinct tiers under one name — and the gap between the bottom and top is a full 4× in nicotine. Here's how to read the hierarchy.</p><h2>CUBA White — 10.4mg/pouch (16mg/g)</h2><p>The entry point, though \"entry\" is relative: 10.4mg is solidly in the strong mainstream, matching the entire 77 range. <a href=\"/product/cuba-white-apple-juice\">CUBA White Apple Juice</a> is the flagship — a genuinely juicy apple profile in a slim 0.65g pouch, 20 per can, with quick 20–40 minute sessions from the moist formula. White is where CUBA competes on flavour first: the retailer copy in our research leads with taste, and mentions strength second. If you're CUBA-curious, start here.</p><h2>CUBA Ninja — 15.6mg/pouch (30mg/g)</h2><p>The middle tier changes the arithmetic in an interesting way: Ninja <em>doubles the concentration</em> (30mg/g vs 16) in a smaller pouch, landing at 15.6mg — and compensates with the best can value in the family, <strong>25 pouches per can</strong> instead of 20. <a href=\"/product/cuba-ninja-mint-fresh\">Ninja Mint Fresh</a> is rated 30–45 minutes (up to 60), and the research's summary line is the tier's whole personality: \"assertive without being aggressive.\" The range is also where CUBA has the most fun — <a href=\"/product/cuba-ninja-strawberry-strong\">Strawberry</a>, Bubble Gum, Energy, Pinacolada, Orange — playful flavours over serious strength.</p><h2>CUBA Black — 43mg/pouch (66mg/g)</h2><p>The top tier is the strongest thing in our catalogue and among the strongest pouches made anywhere: 43mg per pouch, four times the White tier. CUBA labels the range with a skull-adjacent bluntness — <strong>\"Don't Go There\"</strong> — and the visual identity matches: where White and Ninja use white pouches, Black's presentation warns you at every step. The fruit flavours (<a href=\"/product/cuba-black-forest-berries\">Forest Berries</a>, Blueberry, Cherry, Peach and a dozen more) run short, ferocious 20–30 minute sessions; <a href=\"/product/cuba-black-cold-dry\">Cold Dry</a> is the austere mint flagship — dry surface, minimal sweetness, maximum duration for the tier. Black is for a small population of very heavy users. The label means it.</p><h2>The tier logic, summarised</h2><div class=\"overflow-x-auto\"><table><thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>mg/pouch</th><th>mg/g</th><th>Pouches/can</th><th>Session</th><th>Character</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>White</td><td>10.4</td><td>16</td><td>20</td><td>20–40 min</td><td>Flavour-first strong</td></tr><tr><td>Ninja</td><td>15.6</td><td>30</td><td>25</td><td>30–45 min</td><td>Assertive, playful</td></tr><tr><td>Black</td><td>43</td><td>66</td><td>20</td><td>20–30 min</td><td>\"Don't Go There\"</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Moving between tiers</h2><p>White → Ninja is a real but reasonable step (+50% nicotine, softened by faster, shorter sessions and five extra pouches per can). Ninja → Black is not a step — it's a near-tripling, the largest single jump between tiers of any brand we stock. If Ninja has stopped satisfying you, try the ladder outside CUBA first (Pablo Ice Cold at 24mg exists precisely in that gap) before taking the Black label's dare literally.</p><p><strong>Related reading:</strong> <a href=\"/blog/strongest-nicotine-pouches-uk-2025\">Strongest Pouches in the UK 2025</a> · <a href=\"/blog/77-vs-cuba\">77 vs CUBA</a> · <a href=\"/blog/cola-nicotine-pouches-guide\">Cola Nicotine Pouches Guide</a></p>",
  "excerpt": "No brand in our catalogue spans the strength spectrum like CUBA. Nicotobacco Factory (Poland) runs three distinct tiers…",
