  "html": "<p>Mint and berry pay the category's bills — but its soul lives at the weird end of the shelf. These seven are the unusual flavours our research actually rates: strange on paper, convincing under the lip.</p><h2>ACE Eucalyptus — 6mg</h2><p>The category's great herbal outlier. <a href=\"/product/ace-eucalyptus\">ACE Eucalyptus</a> (12mg/g, slim, 20 per can) delivers a balm-like, clearing herbal profile our research file summarises as \"Tiger Balm in pouch form\" — and means it as a compliment. Cooling without menthol's sugar, clean without mint's familiarity. The pouch for people who think they've tried everything.</p><h2>ACE X Guarana Chili Boost — 8mg</h2><p>The maddest entry on any UK pouch shelf: <a href=\"/product/ace-x-guarana-chili-boost\">guarana energy-drink fruitiness with a hot habanero chilli hit</a> (16mg/g). The research copy asks the right question — \"have you ever thought about an all-in-one that goes under your lip with an extra kick?\" — and the answer is that nobody had, which is precisely the appeal. Warmth, fruit and enhanced-release strength in one genuinely unrepeatable profile.</p><h2>Nordic Spirit Elderflower — 9.1mg</h2><p>The elegant one. <a href=\"/search?q=nordic+spirit+elderflower\">Elderflower</a> (14mg/g) is the flavour that made Nordic Spirit's name: floral, lightly sweet, unmistakably Scandinavian — a profile from the cordial bottle rather than the sweetshop, and still without a serious imitator. The unusual flavour you can recommend to anyone.</p><h2>CUBA Ninja Energy — 15.6mg</h2><p>Energy-drink flavour done at proper strength: <a href=\"/product/cuba-ninja-energy-slim-strong\">Ninja Energy</a> (30mg/g, 25 slim pouches) captures the taurine-adjacent sweetness of the canned original and pairs it with CUBA's assertive mid-tier delivery. Of all the novelty profiles, this one converts the most sceptics.</p><h2>Après Lemon Curd — 8.3mg</h2><p>Dessert engineering from Stockholm. <a href=\"/search?q=apres+lemon+curd+extra+strong\">Lemon Curd Extra Strong</a> commits fully to the brief — rich, creamy, citrus-sharp, like the jar and not like lemon candy. Nobody else attempts pudding this literal; Après lands it.</p><h2>Après Ice Tea Peach — 11mg</h2><p>A <a href=\"/search?q=apres+ice+tea+peach+hyper+strong\">chilled black-tea base with ripe peach</a> — crisp, slightly tannic, \"summer in a glass\" at Hyper Strong. The tea's dry brightness is the clever part: it keeps the peach from cloying across a full session. The most sophisticated beverage-pouch made.</p><h2>77 Salted Caramel — 10.4mg</h2><p>The dessert with restraint: <a href=\"/search?q=77+salted+caramel+medium\">rich, creamy, buttery caramel and a refined sea-salt finish</a> — toasted cooked sugar rather than synthetic toffee, per the research consensus. The salt is what elevates it from novelty to rotation regular.</p><h2>How to shop the weird shelf</h2><p>One unusual can per order, alongside your staple — novelty fatigue is real, and even great oddities work best as the third pouch of the day rather than all fifteen. And note what unites these seven: none of them is a joke flavour. Each got the same engineering as the brand's mint. That's the test that separates \"worth trying\" from merely strange.</p><p><strong>Related reading:</strong> <a href=\"/blog/best-berry-nicotine-pouches-uk-2025\">Best Berry Pouches</a> · <a href=\"/blog/cola-nicotine-pouches-guide\">Cola Pouches Guide</a> · <a href=\"/blog/ace-vs-clew\">ACE vs CLEW</a></p>",
