  "html": "<p>Nicotine pouches are small white pouches you place under your upper lip. They contain nicotine, plant-based fibres, flavourings and moisture — and no tobacco leaf. Over a session of roughly 30 to 60 minutes, nicotine absorbs through the gum. No smoke, no vapour, no spitting, and nothing to light.</p><h2>How they differ from snus and cigarettes</h2><p>Nicotine pouches are often confused with Swedish snus, and the format is indeed borrowed from it — but the contents differ fundamentally. Snus contains ground tobacco; pouches use white plant-fibre fill with added nicotine. That's why the category is called \"all-white\": the pouches don't stain teeth the way tobacco portions can, and they carry no tobacco taste unless a brand deliberately adds a tobacco flavouring (like <a href=\"/search?q=77+classic+tobacco+medium\">77 Classic Tobacco</a>, which is tobacco-flavoured but still tobacco-free).</p><p>Against cigarettes the difference is simpler: nothing burns. Pouches are smoke-free and can be used where smoking and vaping aren't possible — offices, flights, public transport.</p><h2>How to use one</h2><p>Take a pouch from the can, place it between your upper lip and gum, and leave it there. That's the whole technique. A tingling or light burning sensation in the first few minutes is normal — that's the nicotine beginning to absorb, and it settles down. Don't chew it, and don't move it around; parked and forgotten is the ideal state.</p><p>When you're done, most cans have a catch lid — a small compartment in the top — for used pouches until you find a bin. Used pouches go in general waste, never down the toilet.</p><h2>What to expect the first time</h2><p>Start low. A 3mg pouch like <a href=\"/product/ace-cool-mint-low\">ACE Cool Mint Low</a> gives you the full experience — flavour, tingle, session arc — at a strength that's forgiving. Sessions typically run 30–45 minutes, though flavour usually fades before the nicotine does. If you feel lightheaded or queasy, take the pouch out; that's the universal signal that the strength or the session length was too much. It passes, and next time you'll know your level.</p><p>Moisture matters more than beginners expect. Moist pouches (like <a href=\"/product/velo-crispy-peppermint\">VELO Crispy Peppermint</a>) release flavour and nicotine quickly; drier pouches like <a href=\"/product/zyn-cool-mint-slim-s3\">ZYN Cool Mint</a> start slower, drip less, and run longer. Neither is better — it's a preference you'll discover.</p><h2>Choosing your first can</h2><p>Three guidelines cover most beginners. First, pick 3–6mg per pouch — you can always step up, but an overwhelming first session is the most common reason people bounce off the category. Second, pick mint: it's the benchmark flavour family and the easiest way to calibrate your palate. Third, pick slim format — it's the most common shape, comfortable under the lip and discreet from the outside.</p><p>After a week you'll know three things: your strength, your session length, and whether you're a mint person or not. From there, the whole catalogue opens up.</p><p><strong>Related reading:</strong> <a href=\"/blog/nicotine-pouch-strength-guide\">Nicotine Pouch Strength Guide</a> · <a href=\"/blog/mini-vs-slim-vs-original\">Mini vs Slim vs Original</a> · <a href=\"/blog/tobacco-free-vs-smoke-free\">Tobacco-Free vs Smoke-Free</a></p>",
