  "html": "<p>The two biggest names in nicotine pouches are both mint-first brands owned by tobacco giants — and they've made opposite bets on how a pouch should behave. ZYN (Swedish Match, Stockholm) bet on dry. VELO (British American Tobacco) bet on moist. That single engineering choice explains almost every difference you'll feel.</p><h2>The heavyweight credentials</h2><p>ZYN's numbers are the category's benchmark: 114.1 million cans sold in 2020, the #1 smokefree brand in Sweden, and global name recognition no rival matches. VELO counters with territory: it claims the <strong>#1 nicotine pouch brand in Scandinavia</strong>, and BAT's distribution puts it everywhere ZYN is. This is Coke and Pepsi, not David and Goliath.</p><h2>Dry vs moist: the real difference</h2><p><strong>ZYN pouches are dry-surfaced.</strong> <a href=\"/product/zyn-cool-mint-slim-s3\">ZYN Cool Mint</a> starts quietly — our research notes cooling activates within about five seconds but builds to peak around eight minutes — then holds for up to 60 minutes with minimal drip. Discretion is the design goal, reinforced by the mini format option (ZYN is the leading mini brand; US mini cans carry 15 pouches vs 20 in standard slims).</p><p><strong>VELO pouches are high-moisture.</strong> <a href=\"/product/velo-crispy-peppermint\">VELO Crispy Peppermint</a> (10mg, 0.7g slim) delivers flavour in the first minute — instant onset is the brand's engineering signature, summarised by its own \"pop, tuck, feel\" language. Sessions run a punchier 30–45 minutes.</p><p>Practical translation: ZYN for long meetings and slow burns; VELO for coffee-break immediacy.</p><h2>Strength ranges</h2><p>ZYN runs a tidy ladder: 3, 6, 9 and 11mg across slim and mini — <a href=\"/product/zyn-spearmint-slim-strong\">ZYN Spearmint</a> at 9mg (13.1mg/g, 21 pouches per can) is the smooth-glide alternative to Cool Mint's cold plunge. VELO's mainstream sits at 6–10.9mg, but its ceiling is higher: <a href=\"/product/velo-freeze-x-strong-eu\">VELO Freeze</a> (10.9mg base) ships 14mg and 17mg variants for users ZYN simply doesn't serve.</p><h2>Flavour range</h2><p>Both are mint empires with a citrus embassy. ZYN's non-mint star is Citrus (the best-known non-minty pouch on the market); VELO's range skews cooling across the board, with Freeze as the strongest menthol experience in either brand's line-up. If you want genuinely un-minty variety, honestly, both giants lose to smaller houses like Après and 77.</p><h2>The verdict</h2><p>Choose <strong>ZYN</strong> if you value discretion, long even sessions, minimal drip, and the reassurance of the category's reference product. Choose <strong>VELO</strong> if you want flavour <em>now</em>, harder cooling, and higher-strength options at the top end. And if you can't choose: a can of each costs less than a takeaway, and your own lip is the only reviewer that counts.</p><p><strong>Related reading:</strong> <a href=\"/blog/mini-vs-slim-vs-original\">Mini vs Slim vs Original</a> · <a href=\"/blog/mint-intensity-map\">The Mint Intensity Map</a> · <a href=\"/blog/apres-vs-zyn\">Après vs ZYN</a></p>",
